The [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] announced Binita Mehta-Parmar as their mayoral candidate in August 2021. Mehta-Parmar was formerly the Conservative group leader on Watford Borough Council.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.watfordobserver.co.uk/news/19509494.watford-conservatives-announce-2022-mayoral-candidate/|title=Watford Conservatives announce 2022 mayoral candidate|date=13 August 2021|access-date=31 March 2022|work=[[Watford Observer]]|first=Nathan|last=Louis}}</ref> Incumbent mayor [[Peter Taylor (mayor)|Peter Taylor]] was unanimously reselected by the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] as their candidate in September 2021. He stated that his priorities would be "to create more jobs, make the town greener and support those most in need."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.watfordobserver.co.uk/news/19586877.liberal-democrats-announce-candidate-mayor-watford/|title=Liberal Democrats announce candidate for Mayor of Watford|date=17 September 2021|access-date=31 March 2021|work=[[Watford Observer]]|first=James|last=Cowen}}</ref> The [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] selected Asif Khan as their candidate in November 2021. Khan is a councillor on Watford Borough Council and Hertfordshire County Council. He stated that he would focus on development in Watford, and was opposed to the number of high-rise buildings under construction.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.watfordobserver.co.uk/news/19733672.asif-khan-selected-labour-candidate-watford-mayor/|title=Asif Khan selected as Labour candidate for Watford mayor|date=23 November 2021|access-date=31 March 2022|work=[[Watford Observer]]|first=Nathan|last=Louis}}</ref>

